+    Plain REINFORCE uses the score grad log p(y) of a token y drawn from the
+    sampler q. On-policy (q = p) that score has zero mean, so only the part of
+    the advantage that depends on y moves the policy. Under q != p its mean is
+    E_q[grad log p] = -grad KL(q || p) != 0, so every token also adds
+    A * (-grad KL(q||p)): a systematic drift that pulls p towards q where A > 0
+    and pushes p away from q where A < 0, growing the mismatch it came from
+    (REPORT.md). This loss subtracts that mean from every token's score, so
+    the per-token score has zero mean under the sampler, as on-policy:
+
+        score_t = m_y log p(y) - sum_{v in K} sg(q_v - p_v) log p(v),
+        m_y = 1 if y in K, else sg(p(y) / q(y)),
+
+    where K is the set of vocabulary ids at which the sampler's distribution q
+    is known at that position:
+      * sampling_vocab_logprobs [B, T, V] (sampler.vocab_logprobs=full): K = V,
+        score gradient = grad log p(y) - E_q[grad log p], no IS weight at all;
+        in logit space the update is exactly q * (A - E_q A), the on-policy
